After the morning meeting, I sit at my desk.
I look at my notes from the presentation.
My boss, Thomas, comes over to me.
He is our project manager.
He has worked here for many years.
"Good morning, Maya," he says with a smile.
"That was a really good presentation."
"Thank you, Thomas," I answer.
He puts a folder on my desk.
It contains my part of the new project.
"You will work on this task," he explains.
I open the folder and look at the papers.
"We are very happy to have you on the team," Thomas continues.
"The whole team has looked forward to working with you."
"I have also looked forward to it," I say happily.
"It is an exciting project."
Thomas smiles again and walks back to his office.
I look at my computer screen.
I feel genuinely welcome on the team.
